IMPORT prelude

-- Compulsory Education Act 2000 (Singapore) -- who is a child of compulsory school age and a "national primary school"
-- (s 2), the duty to attend and each parent's offence (s 3), exemption (s 4), the Board's quorum (s 5(8)), the offences
-- against the Board (s 7(2)) and the penalties (s 7), prosecution only on the Director-General's complaint (s 8), and
-- composition (s 9).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to and including 1 December 2021), informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 9/3/2025", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CEA2000.txt. The latest amendment
-- annotated is Act 5 of 2025 (Electronic Gazette and Legislation Act 2025) wef 09/03/2025, to the definition of
-- "Director-General" in s 2. The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body by one;
-- this file follows the body's numbering (s 3 is the duty, s 7 the penalties).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it is the law that makes primary school compulsory for Singapore
-- citizen children and makes their parents criminally liable for non-attendance. SCOPED to the duty, who bears it, its
-- exceptions, and the offences and penalties. Not encoded: the Board's constitution beyond its quorum (s 5(1)-(7),
-- (9)-(12)), its duties and powers as such (s 6, save that refusing counselling is contrasted with the s 7(2) offences),
-- protection from liability (s 10), the saving of the Education Act 1957 (s 11) and regulations (s 12). The "conditions
-- for receiving primary education" the Director-General may determine, the "prescribed reasons" for absence, any
-- prescribed schools, any exemption orders, and the list of compoundable offences are subsidiary matters that were not
-- retrieved; they are inputs here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following earlier naive rows (the writing-l4-rules skill was not
-- available in the session). No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Compulsory Education Act 2000 -- school attendance`

§§ `2 -- child of compulsory school age`

-- s 2: "'child of compulsory school age' means a child ABOVE THE AGE OF 6 YEARS who has NOT YET ATTAINED THE AGE OF 15
-- YEARS and who satisfies such conditions for receiving primary education as the Director-General may determine".
-- "'primary education' means a 6-year course of education normally commencing when a child has attained the age of 6".
--
-- Age is taken as exact age in years (a fraction allowed). Reading "above the age of 6" as strictly more than 6 is an
-- inference; the text does not say how a child of exactly 6 is treated.
DECLARE Child HAS
    `age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `birth year` IS A NUMBER
    `birth month` IS A NUMBER
    `birth day` IS A NUMBER
    `meets the Director-General's conditions for primary education` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resides in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `attends regularly at a national primary school` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent presented a prescribed reason in reasonable time to the Director-General's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is exempted by Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is of compulsory school age` IF
        `the child`'s `age in years` GREATER THAN 6
    AND `the child`'s `age in years` LESS THAN 15
    AND `the child`'s `meets the Director-General's conditions for primary education`

§§ `2 -- national primary school`

-- s 2: "'national primary school' means any institution for the provision of full-time primary education, being -- (a) a
-- school organised and conducted directly by the Government; (b) a school in receipt of grant-in-aid under the Education
-- Act 1957; (c) a school specified in any order made under section 3(1) of the School Boards (Incorporation) Act 1990; or
-- (d) such other school as may be prescribed".
--
-- That a private or international school, or home-schooling, is not a national primary school unless prescribed is an
-- inference from the closed list; no prescribing regulations were retrieved.
DECLARE School IS ONE OF
    `a Government school`
    `a grant-in-aid school`
    `a school specified under the School Boards (Incorporation) Act order`
    `a school prescribed by regulations`
    `an unprescribed private or international school`
    `home-schooling`

GIVEN `the school` IS A School
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the school is a national primary school` IF
    CONSIDER `the school`
    WHEN `an unprescribed private or international school` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `home-schooling` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2 -- parent`

-- s 2: "'parent', in relation to a child to whom section 3(1) applies, INCLUDES a guardian and any person having the
-- actual custody of the child".
--
-- Mother and father are read in by the ordinary meaning of "parent" (an inference: the definition only says what it
-- includes). A relative without guardianship or actual custody is treated as not a parent (also an inference).
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the mother`
    `the father`
    `a guardian`
    `a person having actual custody`
    `a grandparent without guardianship or custody`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a parent of the child` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a grandparent without guardianship or custody` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3, 4 -- the duty to attend and each parent's offence`

-- s 3(1): "A child of compulsory school age who is -- (a) BORN AFTER 1 JANUARY 1996; (b) a CITIZEN of Singapore; and (c)
-- RESIDING in Singapore, must attend regularly as a pupil at a national primary school."
-- (2): if the child fails to attend regularly, "EACH PARENT of the child shall be guilty of an offence".
-- (3): the section does not apply (a) where "a parent presents within a reasonable time a prescribed reason to the
-- Director-General's satisfaction for the child's absence"; or (b) to a child exempted under s 4.
-- s 4(1): the Minister may by order in the Gazette exempt any child or class of children; (2) an exemption "may be revoked
-- at any time".
--
-- Permanent residents and foreign children are outside s 3(1)(b) altogether. "Born after 1 January 1996" excludes a child
-- born on that day.
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child was born after 1 January 1996` IF
        `the child`'s `birth year` GREATER THAN 1996
    OR  (     `the child`'s `birth year` EQUALS 1996
          AND (`the child`'s `birth month` GREATER THAN 1 OR `the child`'s `birth day` GREATER THAN 1))

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child must attend a national primary school` IF
        `the child is of compulsory school age` `the child`
    AND `the child was born after 1 January 1996` `the child`
    AND `the child`'s `is a citizen of Singapore`
    AND `the child`'s `resides in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the child`'s `a parent presented a prescribed reason in reasonable time to the Director-General's satisfaction`)
    AND (NOT `the child`'s `is exempted by Ministerial order`)

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty under section 3(2)` IF
        `the child must attend a national primary school` `the child`
    AND (NOT `the child`'s `attends regularly at a national primary school`)
    AND `the person is a parent of the child` `the person`

§§ `5(8) -- the Board's quorum`

-- s 5(8): "The quorum for a meeting of the Board is constituted by ONE-HALF of the number of members of the Board."
-- (11): questions are decided by majority of members present, the person presiding having a casting vote.
GIVEN `members of the Board` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` TIMES 2 AT LEAST `members of the Board`

§§ `6(2), 7 -- offences and penalties`

-- s 6(2): the Board may (a) hear witnesses on oath; (b) summon any person; (c) require information or documents; (d)
-- "require any person to attend any counselling or mediation session as the Board may specify".
-- s 7(1): an offence under s 3(2) -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months
-- or to both".
-- s 7(2): any person who "(a) refuses to attend any hearing of the Board; (b) refuses to provide any information or produce
-- any document to the Board; (c) provides any information or produces any document which is false in a material
-- particular and which the person KNOWS to be false or does not believe to be true; or (d) obstructs or impedes the
-- Director-General, the Board or any person acting under the direction of the Board" -- the same $5,000 or 12 months.
--
-- Refusing a counselling or mediation session the Board requires under s 6(2)(d) is not listed in s 7(2). Whether such a
-- refusal could be "obstructs or impedes" under (d) is not settled by the text; it is treated as not an offence here (an
-- inference).
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `failing to send the child to school`
    `refusing to attend a Board hearing`
    `refusing to give information to the Board`
    `knowingly giving false information to the Board`
    `giving false information honestly believed true`
    `obstructing the Board`
    `refusing a counselling session the Board requires`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 7(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `refusing to attend a Board hearing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refusing to give information to the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `knowingly giving false information to the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `obstructing the Board` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is punishable under section 7` IF
        `the conduct is an offence under section 7(2)` `the conduct`
    OR  CONSIDER `the conduct`
        WHEN `failing to send the child to school` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine in dollars` IS
    IF `the conduct is punishable under section 7` `the conduct` THEN 5000 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    IF `the conduct is punishable under section 7` `the conduct` THEN 12 ELSE 0

§§ `8, 9 -- prosecution and composition`

-- s 8: "No person may be charged with any offence under this Act EXCEPT ON THE COMPLAINT OF THE DIRECTOR-GENERAL."
-- s 9: the Director-General "may compound any offence under this Act which is PRESCRIBED as a compoundable offence by
-- collecting ... a sum of money NOT EXCEEDING $2,000".
GIVEN `the Director-General has complained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a charge may be brought` IF
    `the Director-General has complained`

GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the composition sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may compound for that sum` IF
        `the offence is prescribed as compoundable`
    AND `the composition sum` AT MOST 2000
